===Noun===
[[File:Chicken egg01 monovular.jpg|thumb|An egg yolk surrounded by the egg '''white'''.]]
[[File:Cabbagewhite.JPG|thumb|a cabbage '''white''', a ''[[Pieris]]'' butterfly.]]
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[color]]/[[colour]] of [[snow]] or [[milk]]; the colour of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Andrew Martin|title=Underground Overground: A passenger's history of the Tube|publisher=Profile Books, {{ISBN|978-1846684777}}|page=117|text=Not only were the platforms tiled in '''white''', the tunnels were painted '''white''' too - to prettify them, and make them less claustrophobic - and the [[Central]] proudly issued a postcard of its tunnel-whitening machine.}}
# A person of [[European]] descent with light-coloured skin.
#* {{RQ:Doyle Lost World|passage=The Indians carried first our canoes and then our stores through the brushwood, which is very thick at this point, while we four '''whites''', our rifles on our shoulders, walked between them and any danger coming from the woods.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The New Jim Crow|author=Michelle Alexander|year=2012|ISBN=9781595586438|page=54
|passage=The War on Drugs proved popular among key white voters, particularly '''whites''' who remained resentful of black progress, civil rights enforcement, and affirmative action.}}
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:white person}}
# Any [[butterfly]] of the subfamily  [[Pierinae]] in the [[family]] [[w:Pieridae|Pieridae]].
# {{lb|en|countable|and|uncountable}} [[#Adjective|White]] [[wine]].
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1977| title={{w|Scenes from an Italian Restaurant}}| composer={{w|Billy Joel}}| album={{w|The Stranger (album)|The Stranger}}| passage=A bottle of red, a bottle of '''white''' / It all depends upon your appetite / I'll meet you any time you want / In our Italian Restaurant.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2014|author=Maximillian Potter|title=Shadows in the Vineyard
|passage=Those were my first impressions of wine: Ladies drink chilled, soft '''white''' while they gossip in the kitchen; old men drink strong, room-temperature red to get shellacked.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|and|uncountable}} [[#Adjective|White]] [[coffee]]
# {{lb|en|countable}} Any object or substance that is of the color white.
## The [[albumen]] of [[bird]] [[egg]]s (egg white).
## {{lb|en|anatomy}} The [[sclera]], white of the [[eye]].
##* {{RQ:Conrad Heart of Darkness|page=203|passage=You could see from afar the '''white''' of their eyeballs glistening.}}
## {{lb|en|sports|billiards|snooker|pool}} The [[cue ball]] in [[cue]] games.
## {{lb|en|slang|US|UK}} [[cocaine|Cocaine]]
##* {{quote-song|en|passage=I've got to hit the streets; I've got to move this '''white'''.|title=On The Run|year=2004|publisher=Atlantic|artist=Bump J (featuring Rick James)|composer=Kanye West|}}
##*{{quote-av|en|date=2019-01-20|director=Lawrence Gough|writer=Ann Cleeves,Paul Matthew Thompson|actor=Louis Healy|role=Tyler Lennon|medium=TV series|series=9|episode=2|title=Vera(Cuckoo)|time=1:26:51|text=TYLER LENNON(played by Louis Healy): Ten grand a week we were clearing: base, '''white''', meth, weed, anything. I can get you anything to get you high.}}
## The snow- or ice-covered "green" in [[snow golf]].
## A white [[pigment]].
##: ''Venice '''white'''''
## A white [[bean]]
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1952|title=Columbia River and Tributaries, Northwestern United States|publisher=United States Government Printing Office|page=3764|passage=Nearly two-thirds of the Idaho crop has been great northerns, one-sixth small reds, and the remainder small flat '''whites''' and pintos and seed for snap beans and baby limas (table 21).}}
# {{lb|en|archery}} The central part of the [[butt]], which was formerly painted white; the centre of a [[mark]] at which a [[missile]] is shot.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Taming of the Shrew|act=V|scene=ii|passage='Twas I won the wager, though you hit the '''white'''.}}
# The [[enclose]]d part of a [[letter]] of the alphabet, especially when [[handwritten]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1594|author={{w|Hugh Plat}}|title=The Jewell House of Art and Nature|url=https://archive.org/details/b30333404|chapter=38|page=42|location=London
|passage=Also it giueth a great grace to your writing, if the '''whites''' of certeine letters bee made of one equall bignesse with the o. supposing the same were all round, as the '''white''' of the b. of the a. p. y. v. w. x. q. d. g. and s.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1677|author={{w|Hannah Woolley}}|title=The Compleat Servant-Maid|location=London|publisher=T. Passinger|page=18|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A66839.0001.001
|passage={{...}} the a. b. d. g. o. p. q. &c. {{...}} must be made with equal '''whites'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1931|author={{w|Margery Allingham}}|title={{w|Police at the Funeral}}|url=https://archive.org/details/policeatfuneral00alli|chapter=14|page=157|publisher=Penguin|year_published=1939
|passage=She copied the whole alphabet like that, as though only the inside '''whites''' of the letters registered on her mind.}}
# A feather, from the wing of the cock ostrich, that is of the palest possible shade.<ref>{{R:DSAE|white|n|e07865}}</ref>
#: {{syn|en|prime}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Agricultural Journal of the Cape of Good Hope|year=1909|page=514|passage=3.—''Wing-Quills or Remiges''; '''''Whites''' and Feminas.''—The wing-quills are the largest feathers in the wing, and are arranged in a single row. They include the “'''Whites'''” in the cock, and the “Feminas” in the hen, as well as the “Byocks” or “Fancies” in the cock.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Ostrich Feathers of Tripoli|journal=Neenah Daily Times|volume=53|issue=8,451|location=Neenah, Wis.; Menasha, Wis.|date=12 August 1909|column=5|passage=The usual kinds of ostrich feathers known to the trade come into the Tripoli market. These are '''whites''', blacks, feminas, byocks, spadonas, boos, drabs and floss.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=[[w:The Arizona Republic|The Arizona Republican]]|volume=XXI|issue=161|location=Phoenix, Ariz.|date=30 October 1910|page=9|passage='''Whites''', primes, pound, $120 to $300{{...}}The '''whites''' and blacks come from the male birds, the feminas and drabs from the female, the spadones are the first clipping taken from the young birds and the tails from each.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=South African Law Reports. Cape Provincial Division: Decisions of the Supreme Court of South Africa (Cape of Good Hope Provincial Decision).|year=1923|page=532|passage=This parcel included 286 lbs. of feathers known as '''''whites''''', and 211 lbs. of feathers known as ''feminas''. The '''whites''' are described as lot 12, and the feminas as lot 13.}}

